    <item>
      <title>2026.07.28.90531f5</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:29:53 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>20260728.212801</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2026.07.28.90531f5</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
  <li><b>Fixed — the same login in two organizations no longer mixes up its usage.</b> If you imported an account under two organizations (same email, different org), tokenbank could show one org's numbers for the other and even overwrite the saved login. It now tells them apart by organization, so each shows — and keeps — its own. Spotted by The Antwerper Duke.</li>
  <li><b>Accounts show their organization.</b> Each row now lists the organization under the email, so two logins that share an email are easy to tell apart at a glance.</li>
  <li><b>Lighter background helper.</b> tokenbank's daemon is now a native binary — less memory, same features. Nothing to do; it updates in place.</li>
</ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/e-Sensei/tokenbank/releases/download/v2026.07.28.90531f5/Tokenbank-2026.07.28.90531f5.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="EqJaIYgQbobJKpq23Xag4al58Ucg+Imw+hJW0hdPA4IX6dI4WI42Jnb6VJmBleMv4G33JsNBaIPfH2tk6mA1Bw==" length="2551494" type="application/octet-stream"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2026.07.28.f53546e</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 08:54:01 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>20260728.105011</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2026.07.28.f53546e</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
  <li><b>No more spurious "failed" polls when you're offline.</b> Right after waking the laptop, during Power Nap, or with no Wi-Fi, tokenbank now notices the network is unreachable and <b>skips</b> the usage poll (keeping each account's last-known numbers) instead of hanging and logging errors. It refreshes normally the moment you're back online.</li>
</ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/e-Sensei/tokenbank/releases/download/v2026.07.28.f53546e/Tokenbank-2026.07.28.f53546e.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="s3KQmj5L6lO3wawD5rMm4ZvRYvBKW5jfc3boiMPJlwZfveGBahiLy89mlyw6hv1f/kY4Lrlf6YiBctfy4fHyBg==" length="27856648" type="application/octet-stream"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2026.07.28.59f85d3</title>
      <pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 07:25:38 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>20260728.092322</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2026.07.28.59f85d3</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
  <li><b>Fixed — accounts no longer borrow each other's usage after a <code>claude login</code>.</b> If you signed into a different account with <code>claude login</code> (outside tokenbank), the app could show one account's usage for another, and could even overwrite an account's saved login with the other's. tokenbank now detects which account is actually signed in and follows it — moving the "active" marker to match — so every account shows its own usage and keeps its own credential.</li>
</ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/e-Sensei/tokenbank/releases/download/v2026.07.28.59f85d3/Tokenbank-2026.07.28.59f85d3.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="gMoPYCeqg0Qw9KZq6BCnE5B65RVA9GUUXaskTI71TJs7u1Z/Xm0XHe14EV0jTw+V4KpDJigfCsKFDjhTbPJhBw==" length="27856418" type="application/octet-stream"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2026.07.28.00e7803</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 23:01:08 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>20260728.005838</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2026.07.28.00e7803</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
  <li><b>Faster, more reliable usage.</b> Usage now reads each account's plan data directly and in parallel — noticeably quicker, and it can no longer be thrown off by a running Claude session (accounts no longer show each other's numbers).</li>
  <li><b>Claude Code is no longer required just to see usage.</b> tokenbank still shows the detected <code>claude</code> engine in Settings, but polling works without it.</li>
</ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/e-Sensei/tokenbank/releases/download/v2026.07.28.00e7803/Tokenbank-2026.07.28.00e7803.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="0SBDWKylMt0FDr9usJHpU5cFqX6WZYL9gixamNeoX4VoHjDjAQeHg/k6aMQVNd5XVJuXYYPGQX/UJoGqEH7GBA==" length="27856257" type="application/octet-stream"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2026.07.27.864f7a7</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 20:42:19 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>20260727.224004</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2026.07.27.864f7a7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
  <li><b>Fixed — stored logins can no longer be cross-contaminated.</b> A running Claude session could previously cause one account's saved credential to be overwritten with another's during a usage poll (two accounts ending up on the same login). That capture is now skipped while a session is running.</li>
</ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/e-Sensei/tokenbank/releases/download/v2026.07.27.864f7a7/Tokenbank-2026.07.27.864f7a7.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="PnfBDoSBJX7Wdct63xNJBFxYcV8ZVe8gwdKTMXR3HOrE5tPnENamXxFuG3Co+CwNjFbaO36CVQctWOhNRG0eBw==" length="28305323" type="application/octet-stream"/>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>2026.07.27.d8fb537</title>
      <pubDate>Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:55:21 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>20260727.205259</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2026.07.27.d8fb537</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[
<ul>
  <li><b>Fixed — no more duplicated usage bars.</b> When a Claude session is running, tokenbank pauses the background account polls (keeping last-known usage, marked "paused") instead of risking a wrong reading. The active account keeps refreshing, and normal polling resumes once no session is running.</li>
</ul>
      ]]></description>
      <enclosure url="https://github.com/e-Sensei/tokenbank/releases/download/v2026.07.27.d8fb537/Tokenbank-2026.07.27.d8fb537.dmg" sparkle:edSignature="H02oAlX2ZgdUfxzJDTj5ILohh6bogy7+j0VXYaIuDkRBQgCVIEqbuh7foPZ++JtrguW9ODGBd+r0y1mXhIYPAw==" length="28305293" type="application/octet-stream"/>
